      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The average lifespan of polished concrete can be around 10-15 years in a high-traffic area, while luxury vinyl tile (LVT) can last up to 20-25 years. Natural stone, like granite or marble, may last closer to 10-20 years. As for surface damage, you should be most concerned about scratches, scuffs, dents, and wear patterns from high heels and luggage. Additionally, acidic substances like wine and coffee can damage natural stone, and area rugs can be a breeding ground for stains and odors.",
